# How fast can they run?
subtitle: "Place a cheetah, a racehorse, the fastest human and an elephant on a speed line, and see how far apart their top speeds really are."
tags: ["animal speeds","comparative speed","land animals","top speed records"]
teaches: ["concepts/speed-comparison","vocabulary/animal-speeds"]
voices: {"a":"gemini:Fenrir | an excitable quiz host; energetic and playful, still clear","take":"lines"}

## How fast can they run?
sources:
    - id: sharp
      title: Timed running speed of a cheetah (Acinonyx jubatus)
      authors: N. C. C. Sharp
      year: 1997
      doi: 10.1111/j.1469-7998.1997.tb04840.x
      finding: an adult cheetah timed at 29 m/s (about 104 km/h) over 201 m with a running start
    - id: guinness
      title: Fastest speed for a race horse
      authors: Guinness World Records
      year: 2008
      url: https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/fastest-speed-for-a-race-horse
      finding: Winning Brew, 70.76 km/h over a quarter mile, Penn National, 14 May 2008
    - id: bolt
      title: Biomechanical analysis of the sprint and hurdles events at the 2009 IAAF World Championships in Athletics
      authors: R. Graubner, E. Nixdorf
      year: 2011
      finding: Usain Bolt's fastest 20 m in the 9.58 s 100 m reached about 12.3–12.4 m/s (about 44 km/h)
    - id: hutchinson
      title: Are fast-moving elephants really running?
      authors: J. R. Hutchinson, D. Famini, R. Lair, R. Kram
      year: 2003
      doi: 10.1038/422493a
      finding: Asian elephants reached up to 6.8 m/s (25 km/h)

    scale speed cites ["sharp","guinness","bolt","hutchinson"] y 430 unit km/h min 0 max 120 ticks 6 hidden true
    cards runners look flat along speed hidden true
        * "Cheetah" icon.of leopard icon.set twemoji value 104
        * "Racehorse" icon.of horse icon.set twemoji value 71
        * "Usain Bolt" icon.of person-running icon.set fa6-solid value 44
        * "Elephant" icon.of elephant icon.set twemoji value 25
    text unit "km/h" x 915 y 432 font_size 28 hidden true

How fast can animals, and people, run? Here are four runners: a cheetah, a racehorse, the fastest man ever timed, and an elephant.
    draw speed unit runners

    ask "Where does each runner's top speed lie? Drag each card onto the line." on runners store r tolerance 0.08
        right: All {r.total} close.
        wrong: {r} of {r.total} close.

    text v1 "104" #b5482e x 756.6666666666667 y 345 font_size 32

The cheetah is the fastest runner on land: one was timed at about a hundred and four kilometres an hour, over two hundred metres.
    highlight runners_1

    text v2 "71" #b5482e x 564.1666666666667 y 345 font_size 32

A racehorse comes next, though a long way behind. The record, set in 2008, is about seventy-one kilometres an hour over a quarter mile.
    highlight runners_2

    text v3 "44" #b5482e x 406.66666666666663 y 345 font_size 32

Then us. Usain Bolt peaked at about forty-four kilometres an hour during his world record in 2009.
    highlight runners_3

    text v4 "25" #b5482e x 295.83333333333337 y 345 font_size 32

And the elephant is not as slow as it looks: Asian elephants have been timed at twenty-five kilometres an hour, more than twice the pace of an easy jog.
    highlight runners_4

So a cheetah runs more than twice as fast as the fastest person who ever lived.
    highlight runners_1 runners_3
---
